1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,507
Mega Boardgame Con: the best week of gaming, packed with attendees who refuse to

2
00:00:04,507 --> 00:00:04,823
leave.

3
00:00:05,043 --> 00:00:06,792
Here's how the location plays.

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:11,787
Shuffle the twelve Booth cards into a face-down deck, and the ten Booth Event cards

5
00:00:11,787 --> 00:00:12,443
into another.

6
00:00:12,663 --> 00:00:17,122
Add the two Create a Panic cards to the Tableau, and tuck the Finale Reminder card

7
00:00:17,122 --> 00:00:19,297
under the Finale card, reminder side up.

8
00:00:20,133 --> 00:00:24,414
The board has three kinds of area. Exhibit Areas are the yellow booth spaces with

9
00:00:24,414 --> 00:00:27,585
the spade icon. The Food Court is in the bottom left corner.

10
00:00:27,585 --> 00:00:31,760
Everything else is a General Area. There's a key on the back of the rule sheet.

11
00:00:32,567 --> 00:00:36,864
Attendees are having too much fun. No Victim will follow you when you move from an

12
00:00:36,864 --> 00:00:39,223
Exhibit Area space into a General Area space.

13
00:00:39,443 --> 00:00:43,565
To get them out, use Create a Panic to scare them across, or let normal panic move

14
00:00:43,565 --> 00:00:43,816
them.

15
00:00:44,633 --> 00:00:48,636
Create a Panic can only be played in a space with Victims, and you can discard any

16
00:00:48,636 --> 00:00:50,735
Action card in the Action phase to take it.

17
00:00:50,955 --> 00:00:55,403
Two successes: panic each Victim in your space in the direction of your choice.

18
00:00:55,403 --> 00:00:59,176
One success: panic them, but you may change each panic roll by one.

19
00:00:59,176 --> 00:01:02,048
No successes: just panic them. Each costs one Time.

20
00:01:02,867 --> 00:01:07,454
You can search in any space here. Which Item deck you draw from depends on the area:

21
00:01:07,454 --> 00:01:09,693
Exhibit Area, Food Court or General Area.

22
00:01:09,913 --> 00:01:14,236
There are no search icons on the board, but every space counts as a Search space for

23
00:01:14,236 --> 00:01:14,905
card effects.

24
00:01:15,733 --> 00:01:19,617
Hallways and docks are quieter. If you move to a space connected by the blue

25
00:01:19,617 --> 00:01:23,909
double-arrow icon, you get one extra die on the Action card that moves you, but your

26
00:01:23,909 --> 00:01:26,464
first step must be along one of those connections.

27
00:01:26,684 --> 00:01:30,524
And when anyone panics out of the Main Hallway, roll two dice instead of one.

28
00:01:31,333 --> 00:01:33,738
Every Upkeep, draw a Booth card and roll a die.

29
00:01:33,738 --> 00:01:37,676
On one to three, a new attendee arrives: spawn a normal Victim at that booth.

30
00:01:37,676 --> 00:01:40,848
On four to six, draw a Booth Event and apply it at that booth.

31
00:01:41,068 --> 00:01:45,091
If a card only needs a Booth location, just draw the Booth card without rolling.

32
00:01:45,091 --> 00:01:47,404
Reshuffle the discards when the deck runs out.

33
00:01:47,624 --> 00:01:51,777
When the Finale is revealed, flip the Finale Reminder card onto the Booth deck:

34
00:01:51,777 --> 00:01:53,512
no more Booth cards from then on.

35
00:01:54,333 --> 00:01:58,365
Booth Events include Shoulder to Shoulder, a crowd that costs you a die there, Wet

36
00:01:58,365 --> 00:02:01,757
Floor, which stops your movement, and Mega Sale, an extra search die.

37
00:02:01,977 --> 00:02:04,213
And A Lot Going On Today! draws an Event:

38
00:02:04,213 --> 00:02:08,738
with one or no Events in play Horror rises by two, but with two or more you resolve

39
00:02:08,738 --> 00:02:09,828
another Terror card.

40
00:02:10,633 --> 00:02:13,279
A few tips. Don't forget the Booth roll every Upkeep.

41
00:02:13,499 --> 00:02:17,670
Victims in booths won't follow you, so use Create a Panic or the Deodorant to get

42
00:02:17,670 --> 00:02:18,597
them moving first.

43
00:02:18,817 --> 00:02:23,039
Use the hallways for that extra die, and pick the search area whose Item deck you

44
00:02:23,039 --> 00:02:23,873
want. Good luck.

